~ start
Wend WovenWay: The path to Fray's End is through these caves.
Wend WovenWay: The caves are full of StoryVores, I'm sorry to say.
Wend WovenWay: Move quickly, and don't let them spot you!
Wend WovenWay: I'll see you on the other side, StoryWeaver.
=> END

~ walk_through
% Wend WovenWay: You can run by holding Shift or LB!
% Wend WovenWay: Go through the caves, and don't let the StoryVores spot you!
% Wend WovenWay: Watch how the StoryVores patrol, and find spaces to hide.
% Wend WovenWay: You might meet a KnitWitch along the way.
=> END

~ well_done
if memory_thread.revealed:
	=> again
Wend WovenWay: Congratulations, StoryWeaver. You made it through the caves unscathed.
StoryWeaver: Wait, how did you get over here without me seeing you?
Wend WovenWay: Never mind that!
Wend WovenWay: As you go through the world, you'll come across threads of Memory, Imagination, and Spirit.
do wait(0.5)
do memory_thread.reveal()
do wait(0.5)
=> collect_the_thread

~ again
StoryWeaver: But really: how did you get here?
% Wend WovenWay: Sometimes in a game you have to suspend disbelief.
% Wend WovenWay: Check the scene tree in Godot!
% Wend WovenWay: That's for me to know and you to find out.
=> collect_the_thread

~ collect_the_thread
Wend WovenWay: Collect the thread of Memory before we move on!
=> END

~ thread_collected
Wend WovenWay: Onwards!
=> END
